  "body": "`camcraft-ui --headless <file>` now opens the file and draws it in place of the sample document. Before this, the headless start ignored the file without a word (found in the review of #2542).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **The headless entry takes the file list** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/mod.rs`): the same `cli_options::files` and `launch_file::command` as the window (#2462). A refused file (two files, an extension CamCraft does not read, a path that is not a file) is said by name and the run exits with **2**, the code of a bad argument. No adapter is touched.\n- **The file is opened through the same command** (`crates/ui/src/headless_open.rs`, new): `ImportFile` or `OpenProjectFile` on a new state, `State::settle` until the import is done, then `FrameAll`. The seeded proof document is not made.\n- **A file that does not open fails the run** (exit **1**) and names the file: a model file that gives no model geometry, or a project whose open is refused.\n- **The draw** (`egui_app/shell.rs`, `headless::run(open)`): the same View3D readback. The camera is the framed one for a file and the fixed proof vantage for the seed. The 5% pixel check applies when the document has part geometry; a project with no part opens and draws without it. The seeded proof moves to `seeded()` unchanged.\n- **The last line says what was drawn**: `egui shell headless: opened part.stl: 1 model(s), 2 facets, View3D green`; without a file, `seeded document, command world; Contour1 cached 105 moves, View3D green`.\n- **Text**: the `--headless` row of `--help` and of `docs/user-guide/start-options.md` says what a file does. `docs/decisions/2462-open-file-argument.md` points to the new record.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/2648-headless-file.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nmacOS, debug build, `target/debug/camcraft-ui`:\n- `--headless part.stl` (2 facets): `headless snapshot: 320x240, 18% pixels changed`, `opened part.stl: 1 model(s), 2 facets`, rc 0.\n- `--headless examples/first-part.camproj`: `16% pixels changed`, `opened first-part.camproj: 1 model(s), 276 facets`, rc 0.\n- `--headless nope.txt`: `egui shell headless: open refused: nope.txt is not a model or project file (read: .stl, .obj, .step, .stp, .sc, .solidcraft, .camproj)`, rc 2.\n- `--headless` with no file: as before, rc 0.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/ui/tests/egui_app.rs`:\n- `a_headless_start_with_a_model_file_imports_and_draws_it` (rc 0)\n- `a_headless_start_with_a_project_file_opens_and_draws_it` (rc 0)\n- `a_headless_start_refuses_a_file_it_cannot_open_by_name` (wrong extension, missing file: rc 2)\n- `a_headless_start_with_a_broken_model_fails_by_name` (an STL with no facets: rc 1)\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs` `headless_run_succeeds` now calls `headless::run(None)`.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` (the plan from the changed files: ui build, ui lib and 8 ui suites incl. `egui_app`): 10 steps, 0 failed (ui lib: 1216 passed). A first run failed `diag::tests::diag_lines_are_tracing_events_at_their_level` (the INFO line was missing from its captured output); this PR does not touch `diag`, the test passes alone, and the same test failed the same way on another branch's gate. `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test egui_app --test shell`: 8 + 21 passed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and Linux: not run. No platform branches.\n- A `.sc` file headless: not run here (a debug `.sc` import of a large design takes about 100 s); it goes through the same `ImportFile` as `.stl`.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-ui --headless <file>` opens and draws the file, or refuses it by name; it no longer ignores it (#2648).\nEffort: low\nFork synced at v0.24.0 (branch from upstream main 136f19763).\n\nFixes #2648\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01MLU9aif5zm7mure23AKftd\n",
